04:30.120 --> 04:33.320
Sorry, I technically moved this at this point.

04:33.360 --> 04:35.720
We're actually trying to reference this characterList

04:35.720 --> 04:39.600
property, but you'll notice it's gone.

04:39.600 --> 04:41.520
And this is what I was mentioning earlier.

04:41.520 --> 04:43.720
When you have components, the data's

04:43.720 --> 04:46.520
are scoped to the component.

04:46.520 --> 04:48.240
It's not scoped to the entire app.

04:48.240 --> 04:50.280
So in other words, this whole characterList component,

04:50.280 --> 04:53.520
which I made based on impulse, actually,

04:53.520 --> 04:55.960
if we think about Dataflow, it's the wrong way.

04:55.960 --> 04:59.520
Because the characterList is actually basically at the top.

04:59.520 --> 05:02.760
That's the thing that serves everything else.

05:02.760 --> 05:06.480
So let's rethink that over again.

05:06.480 --> 05:08.520
Because what we really want is the ability

05:08.520 --> 05:11.480
to have the app pushed down into a child's components.

05:11.480 --> 05:14.720
Single direction Dataflow is a very big topic these days.

05:14.720 --> 05:16.440
Because it helps to basically ensure

05:16.440 --> 05:17.800
that things are easier to track.

05:17.800 --> 05:19.500
I know that was one of the initial blowbacks

05:19.500 --> 05:21.440
when it came to two-way binding, is

05:21.440 --> 05:24.280
that people were confused about which way data was flowing.

05:24.280 --> 05:25.920
But that doesn't make two-way data binding

05:25.920 --> 05:28.280
like wrong in and of itself.

05:28.280 --> 05:30.480
We can see that when it's done in an encapsulated way,

05:30.480 --> 05:31.840
that's easy to understand.

05:31.840 --> 05:32.560
It's great.

05:32.600 --> 05:34.760
But when it comes to long data flows,

05:34.760 --> 05:37.600
we found as an industry that unidirectional Dataflow,

05:37.600 --> 05:40.680
basically from top down, is keeping that consistent,

05:40.680 --> 05:43.080
for the most part, has been very helpful for making things

05:43.080 --> 05:48.240
maintainable and easier to basically work on.

05:48.240 --> 05:48.920
OK.

05:48.920 --> 05:52.000
